# React testing

`CONTRIBUTING.md` wins if this rule disagrees with it.

## What CI runs

Web unit tests are `pnpm test` from the repo root: `node --test` on `apps/web/src/lib/*.test.ts`. Assert the behavior from those modules (pure helpers, contracts, and source checks the suite already uses). A bug fix adds a regression test on that path when the behavior lives in `src/lib`.

Do not add Jest, Vitest, a component-test renderer, or a numeric coverage gate. A `*.test.tsx` next to a component is not picked up by `pnpm test`.

`pnpm test:e2e` (Playwright) is for a browser flow, layout, drag-and-drop, or the embed iframe. `@axe-core/playwright` is already available for accessibility checks in that suite. End-to-end does not replace `pnpm test`.

## How to assert

- Assert what the operator can observe or what the module returns.
- Do not assert private state, render counts, or which `use*` function ran.
- Do not snapshot whole component trees.
- Changed UI still needs `pnpm lint --max-warnings=0` and, when the build can break, `pnpm build`.
